SUMMARY:America250: Harmony Across Cultures Education Concert
DESCRIPTION:America250: Harmony Across Cultures Education Concert\nOctober 28 at 10:00 a.m.\nMain Stage at Union County Performing Arts Center\nFREE admission\nEducators: CLICK HERE to reserve tickets for your students\nFor more information\, contact info@NJYS.org or call (908) 771-5544 \nNJYS Youth Symphony\nHelen H. Cha-Pyo\, Music Director & Conductor \nTake your students on an exciting\, one-hour musical journey celebrating America’s 250th anniversary! Designed for students in grades 3–8\, this engaging and interactive concert explores how music and dance from many cultures have shaped our nation and continue to bring people together. Under the baton of Helen H. Cha-Pyo\, the New Jersey Youth Symphony joins acclaimed guest artists\, dancers\, and musicians in performances featuring works by Leonard Bernstein\, Raúl Abbad\, John Chance Barnes\, Edmar Castañeda\, Reena Esmail\, Charles Ives\, and more. Through lively audience interaction\, storytelling\, and live demonstrations\, students will discover how music builds bridges across cultures and celebrates our shared humanity. \n \nSupported by funding through the NJEDA’s A.R.T. – Phase II Grant Program.
URL:https://whartonarts.org/calendar/america250-harmony-across-cultures-education-concert/
LOCATION:Union County Performing Arts Center in Rahway\, 1601 Irving St\, Rahway\, New Jersey\, 07065\, United States
CATEGORIES:NJYS,Wharton
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://whartonarts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/October-28-at-10-AM-scaled.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="NJYS":MAILTO:info@NJYS.org
END:VEVENT
